nly one 2 left unknown, so no pair of 2s exists). Playing the Aces guarantees winning the round (unless bombed) and grants the initiative. Gaining the initiative is crucial to play the triplet KKK with a small card (like the 4), effectively reducing the number of difficult small singles in the hand. I also hold the Rocket (Double Joker), ensuring I can regain control if necessary.\n\nReason: Playing the pair of Aces (♠A ♥A) beats the pair of Jacks without breaking the KKK triplet. It is the highest pair available (since pair of 2s is impossible) and secures the lead to transition into a Triplet play (KKK+4), which helps clear the hand structure. Passing risks losing tempo, and playing KK weakens the hand structure significantly.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠A", "♥A"]}'}
